      "retrieved_at": "",
      "difficulty_level": "H2",
      "difficulty_reason": "The full positive-characteristic comparison bridges rational affine-group-scheme cohomology computed in an ind-representation category and cohomology in all stratified sheaves. It requires Frobenius-divided inverse-system/limit control, finite-coefficient extension comparison, injective approximation by finite-dimensional subquotients and filtered-limit arguments to prove all higher groups vanish on proper curves. Original smooth/projective/algebraically closed positive-characteristic/fiber-point/coherent-coefficient scope retained. Old Cartier extension-tower lemma is a later auxiliary construction, not this all-degree comparison. Ind-coefficient/freeness extensions retained without extra counts.",
